  <section id="limits" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
    <h2 id="limits-title">What was tested and what was not</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No Debezium, Kafka, Kafka Connect or database service was run for this page. Every statement about them comes from the documentation linked below, read on 2026-10-09.</li>
      <li>The guarded upsert, the interleaving of backfill and stream rows (all 5,040 orders of seven rows, plus a reversed replay), the idempotent re-run, the sweep and its scoping, the incomplete-key-list hazard, and the counts and suspect-row queries are executed in the site&rsquo;s unit tests on SQLite only. The straddling-transaction case also runs on PGlite when that package is installed, and is skipped otherwise.</li>
      <li>The payload checksum query uses PostgreSQL-only functions, so the SQLite tests cannot run it. It was run once by hand on PGlite, a PostgreSQL-compatible engine. If PGlite becomes a dependency of this site, move the query into the suite. Until then treat it as lightly checked.</li>
      <li>The <code>execute-snapshot</code> example follows the documentation and was not run.</li>
      <li>Check your version: the position that read events carry on PostgreSQL and for incremental snapshots; whether events of a transaction that straddles the boundary carry a higher position; the exact <code>snapshot.mode</code> names on your release; and how your sink treats an equal position.</li>
      <li>Not covered: sizes and prices, connector-specific tuning beyond the properties named above, and backfills of non-relational sources.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

